mini-swe-agent (step 10, $0.01):
The test script confirmed the issue: dict-style access to finished_reason 
returns "interrupted", but attribute access returns "completed" which is the 
dataclass default.

I will fix this by overriding the __getattribute__ method in ChatResponse to 
preferentially return the dictionary key if it exists, falling back to dataclass
attributes otherwise. This will unify the behavior between attribute and dict 
key access.

